<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $142.7 mln May 13.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $142.7 mln May 13.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $142.7 million deficit on May 13 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 13</p>
<p>Exports: $185.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $289.4 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $215.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $254.5 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $142.7 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.920 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.925 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.061 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.056 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.0 billion</p>
<p>NOTE: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
